    "text": "Two coaxial discs, having moments of inertia <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> , are rotating with respective angular velocities <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> , about their common axis. They are brought in contact with each other and thereafter they rotate with a common angular velocity. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math> are the final and initial total energies, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">i</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is:",
